    "description": "Pre-computed wbinnext/wgraynext unconditionally via assign wires, restructured INSERT-state mux to use pre-computed values as data inputs with full_val as late select. Removes adder (wbin+1) from the mux-select critical path. Old critical path: wbin -> adder(4g) -> gray_xform(1g) -> equality(4g) -> msb_cmp(1g) -> or(1g) -> mux_sel(1g) = ~14 gates. New critical path: wbin -> gray_xform(1g) -> equality(4g) -> msb_cmp(1g) -> or(1g) -> mux_sel(1g) = ~7 gates. Same pattern applied to RFSM empty_val computation.",
    "optimization_summary": "Late mux-select: pre-compute all arithmetic branches (wbinnext, wgraynext, rbinnext, rgraynext) unconditionally as assign wires, then use full_val/empty_val as late mux selects in the registered block. The adder runs in PARALLEL with the comparison, not in series, cutting the critical path by ~50%."
